## The Promise Tier

**The Promise Tier** is the $89–$299 range — CZ and moissanite radiant rings where the gesture carries the weight, not the stone itself.

This is not a criticism of these materials. A well-cut radiant CZ in a quality 14K setting looks indistinguishable from a diamond at normal viewing distance and in photos.

Moissanite is closer still — it has real optical properties that approach diamond performance and a hardness that holds up to decades of daily wear. The key difference is durability and what happens to the ring over time.

CZ is rated 8.5 on the Mohs hardness scale. It scratches with daily contact and will begin to cloud within 2–3 years of consistent wear.

Moissanite is rated 9.25 — nearly as hard as diamond — and does not scratch or dull with normal wear. If the ring will be worn daily for more than two years, moissanite is the honest choice in this tier.

### Radiant Cut CZ Promise Ring

A radiant cut CZ ring in sterling silver runs approximately $89–$150 from mainstream retailers. The stone is man-made cubic zirconia — optically bright when new, not a gemstone in the durability sense.

Sterling silver tarnishes and the prongs wear down faster than gold, which accelerates the stone's loosening. For a CZ ring that holds up better, choose 10K or 14K yellow gold — the stone will still scratch over time, but the setting will not discolor and the prongs will hold longer. A 14K CZ radiant ring typically runs $120–$200 total.

CZ is the right choice when the budget is genuinely under $200 and the ring is about the moment, not the material. Do not pretend it is something it is not — and do not give it to someone who will wear it every day for five years.

| Feature | Radiant Cut CZ Ring | What this means |
|---------|---------------------|-----------------|
| Price range | $89–$200 est. | Lowest entry for a radiant cut promise ring. Gesture-first purchase. |
| Stone hardness | 8.5 Mohs | Will scratch with daily wear in 2–3 years. Not a lifetime stone. |
| Appearance | Bright initially, clouds over time | Looks close to a diamond at first glance, especially in photos and at conversation distance. |
| Setting options | Sterling silver, 10K gold, 14K gold | 14K gold setting adds $30–$80 but extends the setting's life significantly. |
| Best for | Early relationships, teenage promise rings, budget-first buyers | If the ring represents "right now" rather than "forever," CZ is the honest choice. |

**Verdict:** CZ radiant rings are appropriate when the commitment is real and the budget is limited. Buy in 14K gold if you expect daily wear for more than one year. In sterling silver, treat it as a 12–18 month ring.

### Radiant Cut Moissanite Promise Ring

Radiant cut moissanite is the strongest alternative to diamond at this price level. Moissanite has a refractive index of 2.65, slightly higher than diamond's 2.42, which means it throws more fire (rainbow dispersion) — some buyers prefer this; others find it too flashy compared to diamond's more restrained sparkle.

A 1ct equivalent radiant moissanite from established retailers (Charles & Colvard, Brilliant Earth, and similar) runs approximately $299–$599 depending on quality and setting. The stone is rated 9.25 Mohs and holds up to daily wear indefinitely — unlike CZ, it does not scratch or cloud with normal use. It will look the same in five years as it does today.

The trade-off is no GIA or IGI certificate and limited resale value. For a promise ring where meaning outweighs origin, moissanite is one of the most honest choices available.

| Feature | Radiant Cut Moissanite Ring | What this means |
|---------|------------------------------|-----------------|
| Price range | $299–$599 (1ct eq. with setting) | Middle tier — diamond appearance, diamond durability, fraction of diamond cost. |
| Stone hardness | 9.25 Mohs | Daily-wear durable. No meaningful scratch risk in normal use. Will not cloud. |
| Appearance | High fire, slightly different sparkle than diamond | Crushed-ice radiant pattern reads like diamond to most eyes at any normal viewing distance. |
| Certificate | Brand certificate, not GIA/IGI | Not a graded gemstone. Appearance is verified, grade is not. |
| Best for | Buyers who want diamond appearance and daily-wear durability at 1/3 the cost | If the look matters and the origin does not, moissanite is the strongest choice in this tier. |

**Verdict:** Radiant cut moissanite is the best choice in The Promise Tier for anyone who plans to wear the ring daily for years. It looks right, holds up, and costs 60–70% less than a lab diamond of comparable size.

