## Lab Diamond Radiant Promise Ring

A lab diamond promise ring is a real diamond ring. The stone is chemically, physically, and optically identical to a mined diamond — it will not scratch, cloud, or yellow with wear — and it comes with an IGI or GIA certificate confirming the exact grade.

Certified market inventory starts at [$867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a [1ct E-VVS1 IGI lab radiant](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). That is a real diamond in a near-top-tier grade for under $900. Adding a [simple 14K solitaire setting](https://www.bluenile.com/build-your-own-ring?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) ([$150–$300](https://www.bluenile.com/build-your-own-ring?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)) brings the total to approximately $1,017–$1,167.

For the highest certified grade at 1ct, the [D-VVS1 IGI at $932](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24946874?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is only $65 more than the E-VVS1. D color, VVS1 clarity — top of the IGI lab spectrum at this size. At a $65 premium, always take the D in lab.

