## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much should a radiant cut promise ring cost?

A radiant cut promise ring costs as little as $89 (CZ in sterling silver) or $1,000+ (lab diamond with setting). The honest range is $89–$300 when the gesture is the point and the budget is real, $867–$1,200 for a real lab diamond promise ring with a 14K setting, or $2,500–$3,100 for a natural diamond. There is no correct number — match the investment to where the relationship is, not where you hope it will be.

### What is a radiant cut promise ring?

A radiant cut promise ring is a promise ring featuring a radiant cut stone — a rectangular or square gem with a hybrid brilliant facet pattern that creates a crushed-ice sparkle. The stone can be cubic zirconia, moissanite, lab diamond, or natural diamond. The radiant cut is a deliberate shape choice: it is specific and recognizable, not the round default.

### Is moissanite a good stone for a promise ring?

Yes — moissanite is one of the best choices for a promise ring if you want diamond appearance and long-term durability without the diamond cost. A 1ct equivalent radiant moissanite runs $299–$599, holds a 9.25 Mohs hardness for daily-wear durability, and is visually similar to diamond at normal viewing distance. The trade-offs are no GIA/IGI certificate and no resale value — both acceptable for a promise ring focused on meaning.

### Is lab diamond better than CZ for a promise ring?

Yes, in almost every case. A lab diamond at [$867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is a real certified diamond — 10 Mohs hardness, IGI certificate, resettable into an engagement ring later. CZ scratches within 2–3 years, carries no certificate, and cannot be reset credibly — if the budget allows $1,000+, lab diamond is the stronger choice in every dimension.

### What does a radiant cut promise ring mean?

A radiant cut promise ring signals serious commitment and deliberate taste. The rectangular shape is not a default — it was chosen. As a promise ring, it typically means "I am committed to you and this is real" without the formal weight of a proposal — the shape itself communicates that the buyer chose this ring specifically.

### What size stone is best for a radiant cut promise ring?

0.75ct is the best size for most promise ring buyers — visible on the hand at conversational distance, wears comfortably for daily use, and does not read as an engagement ring before that conversation happens. A 0.5ct is the subtler choice for early relationships or younger buyers. The 1ct makes sense specifically when you plan to use [The Diamond Bridge](#the-diamond-bridge) strategy and reset the stone into an engagement ring setting later.

### Can a promise ring be a real diamond?

Yes. A lab diamond radiant promise ring starts at [$867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a certified 1ct E-VVS1 IGI stone; a natural diamond starts at [$2,318](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a 1ct G-VS2 GIA. There is no rule that says promise rings must be simulants — a real diamond promise ring is a meaningful choice, especially when using [The Diamond Bridge](#the-diamond-bridge) upgrade strategy.

### What metal is best for a radiant cut promise ring?

14K white gold is the most versatile metal for a radiant cut promise ring — it complements colorless stones (D–G), holds up to daily wear better than sterling silver, and the clean lines work with the radiant's rectangular geometry. Rose gold is the softer choice for a romantic register. Yellow gold works well with G–H color natural stones or any lab color — avoid sterling silver for anything above CZ, as it tarnishes and the prongs wear down faster under a real diamond or moissanite.

### What finger does a promise ring go on?

Promise rings are traditionally worn on the right ring finger. Some people wear them on the left ring finger until an engagement ring replaces them. There is no universal rule — confirm with the recipient which finger they prefer before ordering, since right-hand and left-hand ring finger sizes often differ.

### What is the difference between a promise ring and an engagement ring?

A promise ring signals commitment without a formal marriage proposal. An engagement ring is the formal proposal artifact that precedes marriage and is traditionally worn on the left ring finger.

Promise rings are smaller, less expensive, and carry less social weight. A radiant cut promise ring using [The Diamond Bridge](#the-diamond-bridge) strategy is specifically designed to convert into an engagement ring context when the time comes.

### Can a radiant cut CZ ring pass as a diamond?

At first glance, yes — especially in photos and at normal conversational distances. A well-cut radiant CZ in a quality setting looks similar to a diamond initially. The difference becomes visible under close examination and, more importantly, over time: CZ scratches and clouds with daily wear in a way that diamond and moissanite do not.

For a promise ring worn daily for years, the wear will show. For a ring worn occasionally or for a short period, CZ appearance holds up well.

### How do I upgrade from a radiant cut promise ring to an engagement ring?

If you used a lab or natural diamond promise ring, take the certified stone to a jeweler and have it reset into a new engagement ring setting. The IGI or GIA certificate transfers with the stone.

If you bought CZ or moissanite, the upgrade means replacing the stone entirely — the original ring typically becomes a keepsake rather than a component. This is why [The Diamond Bridge](#the-diamond-bridge) specifies lab diamond: only a certified diamond transfers cleanly into the engagement ring context.

